---
import SealedSection from '../seal/SealedSection.astro';
import SectionHead from '../ui/SectionHead.astro';
import SubHead from '../ui/SubHead.astro';
import Ladder from '../ui/Ladder.astro';
import Limits from '../ui/Limits.astro';
import Shot from '../ui/Shot.astro';
import paneShot from '../../assets/shots/kanban-pane.svg';
import boardShot from '../../assets/shots/kanban-board.svg';

const docBase = 'https://github.com/Vulnetix/belai/blob/main/docs/';

const sealText =
  'Kanban: one global board every Belai session shares, with backlog, review, in_progress, blocked and done. After the report of a work turn the model files what the report left open into review and moves what it finished to done; while it works it keeps its items in_progress or blocked; every call can search and note. An idle empty composer shows the open items colour-coded, and enter fills the composer with a prompt written for that item\'s list. /kanban manages the board, and it syncs with the Belai → Kanban page on the Vulnetix website. Item text is untrusted, so search results always classify and the harness stamps who filed each item.';

const lists = [
  { name: 'backlog', meaning: 'nobody has started it', bar: 'bg-vx-ink/40', prompt: 'start it, do it, verify it, close it' },
  { name: 'review', meaning: 'a session noted it; confirm it first', bar: 'bg-vx-sand-amber', prompt: 'check it is still real before doing anything' },
  { name: 'in_progress', meaning: 'a session is on it now', bar: 'bg-vx-mint-strong', prompt: '' },
  { name: 'blocked', meaning: 'cannot continue; the note says why', bar: 'bg-vx-coral', prompt: 're-check the blocker, then continue or say what still blocks it' },
  { name: 'done', meaning: 'finished and verified, or obsolete', bar: 'bg-vx-mint', prompt: '' },
];

const phases = [
  { n: '01', name: 'Every call', key: 'KanbanSearch · KanbanUpdate', lead: 'In plan mode too. The model can look up an item and add a note to it at any point.' },
  { n: '02', name: 'While it works', key: 'KanbanMove', lead: 'Agent, goal and approved-plan runs move the items they touch: in_progress when they start one, blocked with the reason, done once it is verified.' },
  { n: '03', name: 'After the report', key: 'KanbanAdd', lead: 'One short wrap-up pass files every piece of open work the report mentions into review, and closes what the turn finished. The report stays the answer.' },
];

const triggers = [
  ['unfinished', 'partial work, stubs, placeholders, skipped tests'],
  ['markers', 'TODO, FIXME, XXX and HACK added or found'],
  ['deferred', 'out of scope, follow-ups, phase 2, suggestions'],
  ['unverified', 'tests not run or failing, manual QA, CI red'],
  ['blocked', 'decisions, credentials, upstream, a stalled goal'],
  ['found-not-fixed', 'bugs, vulnerabilities, edge cases, limits'],
  ['temporary', 'workarounds, hard-coded values, debug code'],
  ['tech-debt', 'duplication, refactors, the same fix elsewhere'],
  ['docs', 'README, CHANGELOG, comments, release notes'],
  ['operational', 'deploys, migrations, secrets, monitoring'],
  ['question', 'assumptions, unanswered questions, guesses'],
];

const format = [
  ['BKAN', 'magic'],
  ['version', ''],
  ['gob payload', 'the items'],
  ['SHA-256', 'of the payload'],
];

const limits = [
  ['Item text is classified', "Board items were written by other sessions' models and by people on the web, so `KanbanSearch` results always go through the security classifier."],
  ['Counts, not text', 'The per-turn board facts carry counts and ids, never item text.'],
  ['Stamped by the harness', 'The harness stamps the session, project and directory on each item, and the model cannot set them.'],
  ['Subagents only search', 'Subagents can search the board but never write it, so a poisoned file they read cannot end up there.'],
  ['A bad file is left alone', 'A board file that fails its magic, version or SHA-256 is refused and left as it is.'],
  ['A repository can only turn it off', 'The project layer may turn `kanban` off, never on.'],
];
---

<SealedSection label="kanban" sealText={sealText} id="kanban">
  <SectionHead title="Kanban">
    A report ends with "tests not run", "follow-up: update the docs", "left the workaround in", and the
    next session never sees it. Belai keeps one global board that every session on your machine shares,
    and the model files that open work on it itself. It is also where{' '}
    <a href="#crews" class="text-vx-ink underline">agent crews</a> take their work from.
  </SectionHead>

  <ol class="mt-10 grid list-none gap-3 p-0 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-5" aria-label="The five lists">
    {lists.map((l) => (
      <li class="flex flex-col overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-vx-ink">
        <span class={`h-1.5 ${l.bar}`}></span>
        <div class="flex flex-1 flex-col gap-2 p-4">
          <code class="mono font-semibold">{l.name}</code>
          <p class="text-sm text-vx-ink/75">{l.meaning}</p>
        </div>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ol>

  <Ladder steps={phases} from="reads and notes" to="files what the report left open" />

  <SubHead title="What counts as open work">
    The wrap-up looks for more than the word "TODO". It gives the model eleven categories to look for in
    the report and the conversation, and it searches the board first so nothing is filed twice.
  </SubHead>
  <dl class="mt-8 grid gap-px overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-vx-ink bg-vx-ink/20 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">
    {triggers.map(([name, examples]) => (
      <div class="bg-vx-cream p-4">
        <dt class="mono text-sm font-semibold">{name}</dt>
        <dd class="m-0 mt-1 text-sm text-vx-ink/70">{examples}</dd>
      </div>
    ))}
    <div class="flex items-center bg-vx-ink p-4">
      <p class="mono text-sm text-vx-mint">KanbanSearch first, so nothing is filed twice</p>
    </div>
  </dl>

  <SubHead title="Working an item from the composer">
    When nothing is running and the composer is empty, this project's backlog, review and blocked items
    sit above it, colour-coded. Press <kbd class="mono">↓</kbd> to browse, <kbd class="mono">tab</kbd> to
    filter by list, and <kbd class="mono">enter</kbd> to fill the composer with a prompt written for that
    list. Edit the prompt before you send it.
  </SubHead>
  <div class="mt-8 grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-12">
    <div class="flex min-w-0 flex-col gap-6 lg:col-span-8">
      <Shot src={paneShot.src} alt="The kanban pane above an empty composer, listing review, blocked and backlog items" caption="idle composer, kanban pane focused" />
      <Shot src={boardShot.src} alt="The /kanban board on the review list, with provenance and history" caption="/kanban, the review list" />
    </div>
    <aside class="flex min-w-0 flex-col gap-5 lg:col-span-4">
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-vx-ink p-5">
        <p class="mono text-xs tracking-wider text-vx-ink/60">THE PROMPT ENTER WRITES</p>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-none space-y-3 p-0 text-sm">
          {lists.filter((l) => l.prompt).map((l) => (
            <li class="flex gap-3">
              <span class={`mt-1.5 h-2.5 w-2.5 shrink-0 rounded-sm ${l.bar}`}></span>
              <span><code class="mono font-semibold">{l.name}</code>: {l.prompt}.</span>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-xl bg-vx-ink p-5">
        <p class="mono text-xs tracking-wider text-vx-cream/70">THE WHOLE BOARD</p>
        <pre class="mono mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-vx-mint"><code>/kanban</code></pre>
        <p class="mt-2 flex items-baseline gap-2 text-sm text-vx-cream/80">
          or <kbd class="mono rounded-md border border-b-[3px] border-vx-mint px-1.5 text-vx-mint">f1</kbd> then
          <kbd class="mono rounded-md border border-b-[3px] border-vx-mint px-1.5 text-vx-mint">t</kbd>
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-vx-cream/75">Add, edit, note, move and delete items.</p>
      </div>
    </aside>
  </div>

  <SubHead title="Synced with the Vulnetix website">
    While the Vulnetix CLI is logged in, the board syncs with the <strong>Belai → Kanban</strong> page on
    the Vulnetix website, where you can drag cards between the same colour-coded columns.
  </SubHead>
  <div class="mt-8 grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-2">
    <ol class="m-0 list-none p-0">
      <li class="grid grid-cols-[2rem_minmax(0,1fr)] gap-3 border-b border-vx-ink/20 py-4"><span class="mono text-vx-ink/60">1</span><p>Every change is written to the local file first and pushed in the background, so no tool call waits on the network.</p></li>
      <li class="grid grid-cols-[2rem_minmax(0,1fr)] gap-3 border-b border-vx-ink/20 py-4"><span class="mono text-vx-ink/60">2</span><p>The TUI pulls the web's changes every 15 seconds.</p></li>
      <li class="grid grid-cols-[2rem_minmax(0,1fr)] gap-3 py-4"><span class="mono text-vx-ink/60">3</span><p>The most recent change to an item wins.</p></li>
    </ol>
    <div>
      <p class="mono text-xs tracking-wider text-vx-ink/60">~/.vulnetix/belai/kanban, ONE BINARY FILE</p>
      <ol class="mono mt-3 grid list-none grid-cols-[auto_auto_minmax(0,1fr)_auto] overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-vx-ink p-0 text-sm" aria-label="The board file format">
        {format.map(([part, what], i) => (
          <li class={`border-r border-vx-ink/25 px-3 py-3 last:border-r-0 ${i === 2 ? 'bg-vx-mint/20' : i === 3 ? 'bg-vx-ink text-vx-mint' : 'bg-vx-bone/60'}`}>
            <p class="font-semibold">{part}</p>
            {what && <p class={`mt-1 text-xs ${i === 3 ? 'text-vx-cream/70' : 'text-vx-ink/60'}`}>{what}</p>}
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-vx-ink/75">
        Read <a class="text-vx-ink underline" href={`${docBase}kanban.md`}>docs/kanban.md</a> for the feature
        and <a class="text-vx-ink underline" href={`${docBase}bkan.md`}>docs/bkan.md</a> for the format, byte
        by byte.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <Limits items={limits} class="mt-16" />
</SealedSection>
